{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310594,"nonce":"273YL3RZCHUUptf641IQ2b7WZ00=","title":"FIXED a2385ae0 — every switch over an enum abstract silently took its FIRST case; the name resolver only walked Enum types so `case A:` ...","message":"**THE BUG.** `switch` over an `enum abstract` ALWAYS matched its first case.\nSilent, exit 0, wrong answer, every underlying type:\n\n| subject | got | want |\n|---|---|---|\n| enum abstract Int (0,1,2) | 000 | 012 |\n| enum abstract Int (10,20,30) | 101010 | 102030 |\n| enum abstract String | AAA | ABC |\n| real `enum` | 123 | CORRECT |\n\n**MECHANISM.** `resolve_enum_constructor_from_discriminant`\n(ast_lowering/resolve.rs) walked only `Enum | GenericInstance`, `_ =\u003e None`.\nAn enum abstract is `TypeKind::Abstract` whose values are STATIC FIELDS, so a\nbare `case A:` never resolved; `Pattern::Var` then fell to\n`create_pattern_placeholder_with_bindings` — a CAPTURE, which matches anything.\nFirst arm wins and the rest is folded (MIR for the whole switch was literally\n`$1 = const \"a\"; ret $1`).\n\n**FIXED a2385ae0**: added an `Abstract` arm that looks the name up in\n`class_fields[abstract_symbol]` for a STATIC field.\n**ONLY WHEN THE UNDERLYING TYPE IS A PRIMITIVE** (Int/Float/String/Bool) —\nmeasured: over an ENUM underlying (`enum abstract T(Ordering){var True = GT;}`)\nshort-circuiting to the abstract's own field symbol makes the field unreachable\n(`Cannot access field 'True'`) and REGRESSED Issue11213 PASS -\u003e COMPILE_FAIL.\nFixture `haxe-conformance/regressions/EnumAbstractSwitch.hx` covers Int,\nsparse, String, a default arm, AND a real enum.\n517 -\u003e 518, zero regressions. **The number badly understates it** — the corpus\nbarely exercises enum-abstract switches; the stdlib (Xml.toString) does.\n\n**METHOD — I WASTED FOUR BUILDS GUESSING.** I \"fixed\" three plausible\nalways-true sites in turn (`lower_case_value_pattern` -\u003e Wildcard,\n`lower_parser_pattern_to_hir_with_bindings` Var -\u003e Variable,\n`pattern_to_condition` TypedPattern::Variable) and NONE of them fired. What\nsettled it in one build: tag EVERY candidate site at once with a distinct\n`eprintln`, plus one at the MIR boundary (`lower_pattern_test`). Zero `[pat]`\nlines proved MIR never saw a pattern, which located the collapse upstream.\nSame lesson as [[bugs_generic_call_type_args_never_reached_backend]]:\n**instrument the boundary, and tag all candidates in ONE build.**\n\n**MY FILED ISSUE WAS WRONG AND A SUBAGENT CAUGHT IT.** I filed f119f71 blaming\n`cast this : Self`. A verify agent refuted it with a clean A/B: `cast this : T`\nwith QUALIFIED patterns works, and NO cast with unqualified patterns fails —\nmy original probe confounded the cast form with the pattern form. The cast was\nnever involved. Corrected the issue, then closed it.\n\n**STILL OPEN, filed 9744eba:** `haxe_std_downcast` dereferences a raw scalar.\nThe `(Dynamic, _)` arm of `lower_cast` (mir/expr/casts.rs) emits it without\nchecking whether the register already holds a raw primitive; the sibling\n`(Dynamic, Int)` arm ALREADY guards exactly this. Still SIGSEGVs\n`viaLocalResult` in /tmp/probe/SWABS2.hx. Contributing: `cast this : Kind`\nparses as TWO nested casts and the inner is typed Dynamic because\n`from_context` (ast_lowering/expr/mod.rs) accepts only Class|Interface; the\ncollapse that removes it exists only on the INLINING path, so an inlined call\nis fine and a real one is not.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_enum_abstract_switch_took_first_case` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}